   "id": 530371,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/9be81e565a44d4f7.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work by Chih-chun Janet Lin/ResearchGate)</figcaption>\n</figure>",
   "stem_html": "<p>The phylogenetic tree compares the DNA of some bacteria with the DNA found in mitochondria and chloroplasts.</p>\n<p>What is a conclusion we can reach from this information?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1037436,
     "content_html": "Mitochondria and chloroplasts are closly related to each other."
    },
    {
     "id": 1037437,
     "content_html": "Mitochondria and chloroplasts have a common ancestor, which was a gram negative bacteria."
    },
    {
     "id": 1037438,
     "content_html": "Chloroplasts are closely related to chlamdyia."
    },
    {
     "id": 1037439,
     "content_html": "Mitochondria are closely related to multiple gram positive bacteria."
    }
   ],
